---
// The Privacy page: plain words about what this site keeps. Every sentence describes what the code does today (docs/DECISIONS.md D46).
// It is a plain-words default, not reviewed by a lawyer; the owner chose to open accounts on that basis. Keep it TRUE: if the site starts
// keeping something new, this page changes in the same push.
import LegalShell from '@/components/legal/LegalShell.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
---

<LegalShell title="Privacy" description="What Site Library keeps about you, in plain words." updated="11 November 2026">
	<p>
		{SITE.name} is a free list of useful websites, run by one person (Aditya Rai, India). You can use the whole list without an account.
		This page says exactly what is kept when you do and when you do not.
	</p>

	<h2>If you do not sign in</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Page views.</strong> The home page adds one to a single total. No IP address, cookie or ID is stored for this. Only the total is kept.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Your colour and dark-mode choice</strong> is kept in your own browser. It is never sent to us.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Our website host, Cloudflare,</strong> delivers every page, so it sees technical data such as your IP address, as any host does. We do
			not receive or keep that. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
		</li>
		<li>We use <strong>no advertising, no analytics and no tracking cookies</strong>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>If you sign in</h2>
	<p>You sign in with Google or GitHub. We never see or store a password.</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>What we get from them:</strong> your email address, your name and the address of your profile picture, a unique sign-in ID and which
			one you used. The name and picture are shown only to you, in the sidebar. Nobody else sees them.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>What you add:</strong> the websites you bookmark, the star ratings you give and the written reviews you write, each linked to your account.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Who can see your bookmarks and ratings:</strong> only you. The database refuses anyone else, and that is tested. The person who runs the
			database (the owner) can see them in its dashboard. Everyone sees only the totals for each website, such as "4.5 from 12 ratings", never who gave them.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Written reviews:</strong> a review is plain text. The owner reads each new or changed review and approves it before anyone else can see it.
			Once approved, everyone can read it on that website's feedback panel, with the date and without your name. The owner can still see who wrote it,
			and can remove it. You can change or delete your review at any time. A changed review waits to be approved again.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Your browser</strong> keeps your sign-in in its local storage, so you stay signed in until you sign out.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Google and GitHub</strong> learn that you signed in to {SITE.name}. Their own policies apply to them:
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google</a> and
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Where it is stored</h2>
	<p>
		Accounts, bookmarks, ratings and reviews are stored with <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase</a>, our database
		provider, on Amazon Web Services in Tokyo, Japan.
	</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>See your data:</strong> open your name in the sidebar of the list page and choose "Download my data".</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Delete it:</strong> choose "Delete my account" in the same place. Your account, your bookmarks, your ratings and your reviews are deleted at once.
			Backups kept by our database provider may hold a copy for a while. We have not confirmed for how long.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Questions or a problem:</strong> message <a href={SITE.xUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">@Adicrux on X</a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Who can have an account</h2>
	<p>
		You need to be old enough to have a Google or GitHub account where you live. Reading the list needs no account at any age.
	</p>

	<h2>Other websites</h2>
	<p>The websites we list are other people's sites with their own privacy rules. A link leaves {SITE.name}.</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>When what we keep changes, this page changes in the same update, and the date at the top changes with it.</p>
</LegalShell>
